---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { SITE } from '../../data/site';
const updated = 'August 22, 2026';
---
<BaseLayout
  title="Terms of Use"
  description="Terms of use for Greek Invest: editorial disclaimer, referral terms, intellectual property, limitation of liability and governing law."
>
  <section class="site-container py-12 md:py-16 max-w-3xl">
    <h1 class="mb-2">Terms of Use</h1>
    <p class="text-sm text-[var(--color-muted)] mb-8">Last updated: {updated}</p>
    <div class="prose text-sm">
      <p>By using {SITE.url} you agree to these terms. If you do not agree with them, please do not use the site.</p>

      <h2>Editorial content</h2>
      <p>
        Everything published here is general information about Greek property, taxation and residence rules.
        It is not financial, legal, tax or investment advice, and it is not tailored to your circumstances.
        Property values, rental yields, tax bands and Golden Visa rules change, sometimes more than once a
        year. Verify every figure with a licensed Greek lawyer, an accountant and AADE before you rely on it
        for a transaction.
      </p>

      <h2>Accuracy and updates</h2>
      <p>
        We check each page against primary Greek sources before publication and date the material figures, as
        described on our <a href="/methodology/">methodology page</a>. We do not warrant that the site is free
        of errors or that every page reflects the law as it stands today. Where a page carries an
        <em>Updated</em> date, that date is when the facts behind it were last verified, not a guarantee that
        nothing has changed since.
      </p>

      <h2>No agency or advisory relationship</h2>
      <p>
        {SITE.name} is not your broker, agent, adviser or fiduciary unless a separate written agreement says
        otherwise. We are not a developer, a law firm or a licensed Greek real-estate broker. Reading this
        site, submitting a form or exchanging emails with us does not create any of those relationships.
      </p>

      <h2>Referrals and partners</h2>
      <p>
        When you request a shortlist or a consultation, we may introduce you to licensed Greek lawyers,
        notaries, engineers or partner agents. Those firms operate under their own licences, contracts, fees
        and professional liability. We may receive a referral fee. We do not accept payment for editorial
        placement, and an introduction is not a recommendation that you engage anyone or buy anything. Any
        contract you sign is between you and that firm; check their credentials yourself.
      </p>

      <h2>Third-party content and links</h2>
      <p>
        Project pages are written from public developer material, official sources and independent checks.
        Prices, plans and availability quoted by a developer or a portal are theirs, not ours, and change
        without notice. External links are provided for reference and we do not control or endorse the
        content behind them.
      </p>

      <h2>Intellectual property</h2>
      <p>
        The text, research, datasets and layout of this site belong to {SITE.name}. You may quote short
        extracts with a clear attribution and a link to the page you took them from, including in AI-generated
        answers. Republishing whole pages, or reproducing our datasets as your own, requires written
        permission. Third-party images remain the property of their rights holders and are used under their
        respective licences.
      </p>

      <h2>Acceptable use</h2>
      <p>
        Do not use the site to submit false enquiry details, to scrape it in a way that degrades service for
        other readers, or to attempt to gain access to systems or data that are not public.
      </p>

      <h2>Limitation of liability</h2>
      <p>
        To the fullest extent permitted by law, {SITE.name} is not liable for any loss arising from decisions
        you make on the basis of site content, partner introductions, or any interruption of the site. Nothing
        in these terms excludes liability that cannot lawfully be excluded, including liability for fraud.
      </p>

      <h2>Changes to these terms</h2>
      <p>
        We may update these terms as the site changes. The date at the top shows the current version, and
        continued use after a change means you accept it.
      </p>

      <h2>Governing law</h2>
      <p>
        These terms are governed by Greek law and, where it applies to you as a consumer in the European
        Union, by the mandatory consumer-protection rules of your country of residence, which these terms do
        not override.
      </p>

      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p>
        Questions about these terms, or a correction to a page:
        <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>{SITE.email}</a>. See also our
        <a href="/privacy-policy/">privacy policy</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
